z(7,'explanation','The main privilege mismatch is the deprivileged guest kernel. Normal user instructions can execute directly; this does not promise undetectable virtualisation.','Remove universal every-instruction equivalence.',[a],1)
z(7,'workedExample','A guest kernel expects privileged operations to affect its virtual machine, so software virtualisation must intercept or translate those operations. Application code normally expects user privilege already. The VMM can execute that code directly while controlling mappings and handling exceptions; timing and some machine observations can still differ.','Qualify direct execution.',[a])
