z(9,'explanation','Correct for this historical comparison. Adaptive translation replaced repeatedly trapped page-table accesses with callouts; early hardware execution continued to incur costly transitions and shadow-state handling.','Keep hardware costs specific to measured implementation.',[a],2)
z(9,'workedExample','The paper\'s forkwait benchmark stresses process creation and shadow-page-table work. Its adaptive software VMM avoids many repeated traps by rewriting offending instructions; its early hardware VMM pays entry/exit and state-reconstruction costs. This explains that result, not a universal ordering for all later CPUs or workloads.', 'Avoid each-page-write universal and categorical later reversed result.',[a])
